(5688, 'ZBS-3015', 'LUZON', 'REGION III', 'ZAMBALES', 'SANTA CRUZ', 'GUINABON', 2008, 15.81076188, '15° 48\' 38.742768\"', 119.98548880, '119° 59\' 7.759680\"', 'ZBS-3015 Station is located in Brgy. Guinabon, Sta. Cruz, Zambales. It is located inside the lot owned by the Meradios Family. It is about 50 m N of the house of Jenaro Meradios, and on the opposite side of the dirt road from the houses of Alex and Arnel Meradios. It is about 100 m E of the Nayon River. Mark is the head of a 4 in. copper nail, set in a 25 cm x 25 cm concrete monument, set flush to the ground, with inscription, \"ZBS-3015, 2007, NAMRIA\".', 2007, 'PRS92 Densification', 0.00, 15.81076188, '15° 48\' 38.742760\"', 119.98548880, '119° 59\' 7.759670\"', 0.0000, '0', 61.5770, 0.0000, '4', 19.2027, 819845.13470, 1750275.00200, '50', 15.81236642, '15° 48\' 44.519120\"', 119.98415660, '119° 59\' 2.963750\"', 24.0465, 1748948.72500, 391168.00500, '3', 819704.14400, 1750343.85900, '50', 0.00000000, '0° 0\' 0.000000\"', 0.00000000, '0° 0\' 0.000000\"', 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, '1999-01-01', 'TIM', '2022-01-01 00:00:00', ''),
