(12115, 'NGW-6', 'VISAYAS', 'NIR', 'NEGROS OCCIDENTAL', 'CITY OF SAGAY', 'OLD SAGAY', 1989, 10.90688791, '10° 54\' 24.796490\"', 123.41742610, '123° 25\' 2.734080\"', 'NGW-6 From Bacolod City Capitol building, travel northward along the national highway towards New Sagay, about 81.7 km. or 1.20 hours up to Sagay municipal building. From there, proceed for about 100 meters, then turn left towards Old Sagay. At this junction the water tank is already visible. Travel northward for about 900 meters up to the base of the water tank. The station is located on the center top of a 30.52 meters high concrete water tank inside the compound of Sagay Water District. Station mark is a cross cut on top of a 0.15 m. x 0.01 m diameter brass rod set in a drill hole, centered on a cement patty level to the concrete surface, center top of water tank and inscribed with station name and number. Sub-surface mark; none. Reference marks; none.', 2007, 'PRS92 Densification', 0.00, 10.90688791, '10° 54\' 24.796490\"', 123.41742610, '123° 25\' 2.734080\"', 0.0000, '0', 125.9488, 0.0000, '1', 64.7316, 545615.86420, 1205715.45900, '51', 10.90808752, '10° 54\' 29.115070\"', 123.41598210, '123° 24\' 57.535490\"', 66.7960, 1206194.63700, 545474.34700, '4', 545458.43000, 1205772.44800, '51', 0.00000000, '0° 0\' 0.000000\"', 0.00000000, '0° 0\' 0.000000\"', 0.0000, 0.0000, 0.0000, '1991-01-01', 'Jay Cepe', '2021-01-01 00:00:00', ''),
